This product is an independent, from-scratch implementation of the real-time
detection, instance-segmentation, and oriented-detection methods described in
the Ultralytics YOLO26 paper (arXiv:2606.03748), built on PyTorch Lightning
and licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

"YOLO" refers to the family of real-time object detectors originated by
Joseph Redmon et al., "You Only Look Once: Unified, Real-Time Object
Detection" (arXiv:1506.02640, CVPR 2016), whose original Darknet
implementation is MIT-licensed. The term is used here as a model-family
category name, consistent with a decade of multi-party usage (YOLOX, YOLOv6,
YOLOv7/v9, PP-YOLOE, YOLO-NAS, and others).

This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or derived from Ultralytics
or its codebase. No Ultralytics source code, configuration files, or model
weights were consulted or used at any point. The clean-room provenance record
lives in docs/PROVENANCE.md.
